# Performance Rules

## Core Budgets
- Initial route render SHOULD complete in under 2s on a standard developer laptop.
- Interactive list/table views MUST avoid unnecessary full-tree re-renders.
- Expensive computations MUST be memoized or moved outside render paths.

## React and Zustand Patterns
- MUST use store selectors (`useTasheelStore(s => s.slice)`) instead of full-store subscriptions.
- MUST avoid inline object/array creation in deeply repeated render paths when avoidable.
- SHOULD use `useMemo`/`useCallback` only when they prevent measurable re-render cost.

## UI Rendering Rules
- Tables with potentially large datasets MUST include pagination or virtualization strategy.
- Workflow and form-builder canvases MUST clean up subscriptions/listeners on unmount.
- Icons, badges, and status components SHOULD be lightweight wrappers around shadcn primitives.

## Non-Negotiable Rules
- MUST not introduce blocking synchronous loops in render or event handlers.
- MUST not perform date parsing/formatting repeatedly inside tight map loops without caching.
- MUST verify no memory leaks for bpmn-js modeler lifecycle and drag-and-drop listeners.

## Definition of Done for Performance
1. No obvious unnecessary re-renders in modified components
2. No long-running work in render body
3. No leaked modeler/listener/timer instances
4. Key list/canvas interactions remain responsive
